==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Teacher Bear]]s spawn, delay 40~53.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 8~12 seconds<sup>240f~360f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 3~6 seconds<sup>90f~180f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 8~12 seconds<sup>240f~360f</sup>.
**1 [[Teacher Bear]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 8~12 seconds<sup>240f~360f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Arguably the hardest stage in the sub-chapter, the Teacher Bears in this stage have only 36,000 health, but 12,000 attack power, making it so almost any low leveled meatshield can get shredded instantly. Combined with the fact that they can stack up easily due to their pretty average delay for boss-like enemies, which makes them even more formidable when stacked.

With that being said, it is advisable to at least have some [[:Category:Crazed Cats|Crazed Cats]] when attempting this, [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank Cat]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]] and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Lizard Cat]] being the best for this stage in particular. Having a high enough leveled [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]] to survive a hit from the Teacher Bears is also pretty essential if not using any Crazed Cats.

During the battle, you also want to make sure you manage your money wisely enough to spawn enough rangers to attack the Teacher Bears, as your only real sources of money come from the Teacher Bears and the Doge Darks. This can be difficult at times, but as with most stages, [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] can make this stage a lot easier.

